---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "About Me";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <p>
    Every product reaches a point where things feel heavier than they should.
    Performance dips. Architecture gets fuzzy. The roadmap slows down. I've
    always been drawn to those moments — the places where clarity, structure,
    and thoughtful engineering can unlock momentum again.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm a technical advisor and engineer who helps teams build fast, reliable,
    maintainable products. My work sits at the intersection of performance,
    architecture, and developer experience. I care deeply about systems that
    feel good to work on and products that feel great to use.
  </p>
  <h2>My Approach</h2>
  <p>
    I believe good engineering is calm, intentional, and collaborative. I don't
    show up with a rigid framework or a one‑size‑fits‑all playbook. Instead, I
    work closely with your team to understand how things actually work today —
    the constraints, the trade‑offs, the hidden complexity — and then help you
    move toward a simpler, more reliable future. My focus is always on:
    <ul>
      <li>Clarity over cleverness</li>
      <li>Long‑term maintainability over quick hacks</li>
      <li>Practical solutions over theoretical purity</li>
      <li>Empowering teams rather than creating dependency</li>
    </ul>
    I want your team to feel more confident, not more overwhelmed.
  </p>
  <h2>Where I Come From</h2>
  <p>
    I've spent years building and improving complex systems — from creative
    tools and real‑time graphics pipelines to large React/Node.js applications
    and fast‑moving startup products. I've been the person fixing the
    performance issues no one else could reproduce, untangling the architecture
    that grew too quickly, and smoothing out the release processes that slowed
    teams down. Along the way, I've developed a deep appreciation for:
    <ul>
      <li>Clean, intentional architecture</li>
      <li>Fast, predictable performance</li>
      <li>Developer workflows that reduce friction</li>
      <li>Tools that empower creativity</li>
      <li>Systems that scale without becoming brittle</li>
    </ul>
    These aren't just technical preferences — they're the foundation of products that
    last.
  </p>
  <h2>How I Think About Engineering</h2>
  <p>
    To me, engineering is a craft. It's not just about writing code; it's about
    shaping systems that support the people who build them and the people who
    use them. I'm happiest when I'm helping teams:
    <ul>
      <li>Understand the real root cause of a problem</li>
      <li>Make decisions with clarity instead of guesswork</li>
      <li>Build features without creating future chaos</li>
      <li>Improve performance in ways that actually matter</li>
      <li>Create workflows that make shipping feel effortless</li>
    </ul>
    Good engineering creates momentum. My work is about restoring that momentum when
    it starts to slip.
  </p>
  <h2>Outside the Work</h2>
  <p>
    I'm endlessly curious about creative tooling, generative visuals, and the
    intersection of art and engineering. I love building tools that empower
    creators, exploring new rendering techniques, and experimenting with ways to
    make complex systems feel intuitive.
  </p>
    <p>
    That curiosity shapes how I work: always learning, always refining, always
    looking for the simplest path that still respects the complexity of the
    problem.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
